- Motivation
    Solution Architect
        target
        actual
        - shared understanding
            target: functional rationale understanding between reader and writer
            actual: contention or malfunction of of functional understanding
            - balanced rationale
                target: functional rationale don't contradict itself
                actual: inconsistent and contradictory rationales
                - understanding of paradigm elements
                    target: function objectives and types are well remembered elements of thought
                    actual: new way of thinking causes it's own problems
                - natural objective decomposition
                    target: first objective and last objective logically follows parent
                    actual: unnatural functional decomposition
                - type decomposition resonates
                    target: higher order types are better
                    actual: ...
                - peer objective cohesion
                    target: peer child objective follows "magic formula" to achieve parent objective
                    actual: unclear or ambiguous functions defined and links not clear
            - Consistent rationales
                - Use of motivational rationale to come up with grandparent objective
                - inputs, outputs and qualified objectives share entity model
            - scope of what must be done is integrated
                target: full content derived to most useful level with sharp boundaries
                actual: specific high coupling viewpoint bais
            - terminology defined
                target: specific reader terms integrated into standardised industry terminology
                actual: different understanding of function between reader and writer
    Reader
        - essential elements evaluation against motivation
        - identify outputs required
        - intrinsic dependencies
